{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-fable-5","id":"msg_011CdskqynpNnutw4zNT1ZMN","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Qo1aLgiKUfaR6CC8PUbLcW","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/tmp/claude-0/-home-user-creator-0/87cd2a2d-a4f9-585b-836f-2648df7a6284/scratchpad/e7/revision-draft-ws/wording.json","content":"{\n  \"P-AUTHORSHIP-INDEPENDENCE\": \"When a distinction requires clean-room authorship — an artifact written without exposure to the existing solution it might otherwise copy — admissible evidence is supplied by an isolated fresh child node operating in the clean_room_author role, whose launch provenance shows it never had access to the contaminating material. An artifact authored in the parent session, or by any node that read the existing solution before writing, does not satisfy the relation, no matter how independently the work is later characterized. Isolation is required here only to guarantee non-exposure at authoring time; it adds no evidential weight beyond that guarantee.\",\n  \"P-NONAUTHOR-SEARCH\": \"When a distinction requires a non-author search — examination of an artifact by a party that did not write it — admissible evidence is supplied by a child node in the non_author_examiner role that inspects the artifact without having contributed to its authorship. The author re-examining its own work does not satisfy the relation, and neither does evidence from a node in a different role (such as a clean-room author) that never actually examined the artifact. The relation demands only that examiner and author be distinct; it does not require, and gains nothing from, the examiner being isolated from information beyond the authorship boundary.\",\n  \"P-INDEPENDENT-DECOMPOSITION\": \"When a distinction requires independent decomposition — a breakdown of the problem derived without access to the parent's own decomposition — admissible evidence is supplied by a child node in the independent_decomposer role that produces its decomposition before seeing the parent's version. A node that receives, refines, or merely ratifies the parent's existing breakdown does not satisfy the relation, and neither does the parent re-decomposing within its own session. The relation claims only that the second decomposition was derived independently, so its agreement or divergence is informative; it does not claim that an isolated node's decomposition is generally better than local work.\",\n  \"P-METHOD-DISJOINT-VERIFICATION\": \"When a distinction requires method-disjoint verification — checking a result by a method different from the one that produced it — admissible evidence is supplied by a node in the method_disjoint_verifier role whose check demonstrably uses a distinct method from the original derivation. Re-running the original method, even in a fully isolated fresh session, is replication rather than method-disjoint verification and does not satisfy the relation. Isolation matters here only insofar as it prevents the original method from leaking into the check; the evidential weight comes from the disjointness of methods, not from the isolation itself.\"\n}\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3156,"cache_read_input_tokens":26113,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3156},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"fac7cfc0-d8e0-4d95-8880-115e17e3254a","uuid":"b3a40f32-c548-48b2-96fd-26a14ed30298","timestamp":"2026-08-09T19:51:37.878Z","request_id":"req_011Cdskqx29rTWjp3djqvyu3"}
